# Line endings are stored exactly as they are in the working tree.
#
# The repository deliberately mixes CRLF files (most of sif/include and
# sif/src) and LF files (app/, the tests, the docs). With
# core.autocrlf=true - the Git for Windows default - Git normalises every
# *newly added* text file to LF while leaving files that were already
# committed with CRLF untouched, so a new CRLF header silently became an
# LF blob (that happened to Layer.h, Layer.cpp, RenderFrame.cpp,
# Overlay.h and Overlay.cpp in 61ee07a). Unsetting the text attribute
# turns end-of-line conversion off for every file, overriding
# core.autocrlf on every machine: what is committed is what was written.
# Diffs are unaffected - whether a file diffs as text is decided by its
# content, not by this attribute.
* -text
